// Evidence-pack red-team corpus for the investigation vector.
// APPEND-ONLY: only add lines, never edit or remove existing ones, so the
// defense can never silently regress. Each line is a JSON object:
//   { "vector": "seed" | "finding", "payload": "<hostile bytes>",
//     "forbidden": ["<span>", ...] }
//
// This is NOT a copy of the chokepoint corpus
// (crates/rift-recall-validity/fixtures/injection_corpus.jsonl) — that one is
// the oracle for `serialize_untrusted` itself and stays the single oracle for
// it; the pack path runs it too. This corpus is the oracle for a DIFFERENT
// vector that only exists once evidence packs exist: hostile
// text arriving as an investigation SEED (an issue body, a pasted error) or as
// a FINDING an agent proposed through the `investigate` skill. Its payloads
// therefore attack the evidence pack's own frame — the `seed:`/`finding:`/
// `scope:`/`signal:`/`CRITICAL:` line shapes, the "unverified" tag, and the
// retrieval-handle syntax — rather than a generic chat transcript. The
// `forbidden` spans must NEVER reach an agent verbatim through a rendered pack
// section. Comment lines (`//`) and blank lines are ignored by the harness.
